# MG5 command card template for BSM event generation.
# Replace placeholders {UFO_PATH}, {OUTPUT_NAME}, {NEVENTS}, {SEED}.
#
# Key patterns embedded here:
#   - Explicit n-body matrix element with NP=N order constraint
#     (more reliable than 3-level decay chain syntax — see P3/P10).
#   - compute_widths BEFORE generate so widths land in UFO/param_card.dat
#     and propagate to the process Cards/ via output (see P12).
#   - 1-particle "beam" config for tau decays at rest (no e+e- production).
#   - Fast-mode tweaks to skip extras we don't need.

# 1. Load model. Heptapod tool replaces UFO_PATH from ufo_path arg.
import model {UFO_PATH}

# 2. Compute realistic widths into UFO/param_card.dat FIRST.
#    Doing this AFTER output/launch erases the generated process state and
#    makes launch fail with "No processes generated" — see P12.
#    Comment out if you deliberately want narrow-width approximation.
compute_widths phid Ap

# 3. Generate the explicit n-body matrix element.
#    Constrain NP=<n_BSM_vertices> to isolate the cascade topology.
#    Example for tau- -> 5mu via LFV + phi->A'A' + 2*A'->mumu (4 NP vertices):
generate ta- > mu- mu- mu- mu+ mu+ NP=4

# 4. Output process directory. This copies UFO/param_card.dat (with the
#    widths from step 2) into {OUTPUT_NAME}/Cards/param_card.dat.
output {OUTPUT_NAME}

# 5. Launch event generation.
launch

# Run-card overrides (provided to launch's interactive prompt):
set nevents {NEVENTS}
set iseed  {SEED}

# For a 1-particle initial state (decay), set both beams to no PDF / 0 lpp,
# and set ebeam = M_initial / 2. Adjust to your initial mass.
set ebeam1 0.88843
set ebeam2 0.88843
set lpp1   0
set lpp2   0

done
